From: Ahrion Gallegos <ahrionmgallegos@gmail.com>
Subject: net: wwan: mhi_wwan_mbim: native XDP hook on the RX datagram path

Stage 2 on top of the gro_cells conversion (991): run an attached XDP
program on every de-aggregated MBIM datagram, before GRO/stack
delivery. Implements ndo_bpf (XDP_SETUP_PROG), a per-link rcu-protected
prog pointer, an xdp_rxq_info registered per link netdev, and
NETDEV_XDP_ACT_BASIC advertisement so ip/libxdp attach in driver mode.
The xdp_rxq_info is registered from ndo_init and torn down in ndo_uninit,
alongside the gro_cells 991 put there, so the core unwinds both on a
failed register_netdevice() and neither newlink nor dellink needs an
error ladder of its own.

Honest ceiling, by design: MBIM NTB aggregation means datagrams share
one 32KB DMA buffer, so each is copied out before the program runs —
this hook buys the earliest possible drop point and driver-context
filtering, not the zero-copy page-flip fast path XDP has on real NICs.
Verdicts: XDP_PASS (head/tail/meta adjustments propagated to the skb),
XDP_DROP/XDP_ABORTED (counted in rx_errors, traced), XDP_TX (reflected
via dev_queue_xmit, so the egress qdisc still applies). XDP_REDIRECT is
intentionally not implemented (it would bypass the shaper); it warns
and drops. When no program is attached the cost is one rcu_dereference
per datagram.

The program run is bracketed by bpf_net_ctx_set()/bpf_net_ctx_clear().
Since 401cb7dae813 the redirect helpers read struct bpf_redirect_info
out of current->bpf_net_context, and bpf_net_ctx_get_ri() dereferences
that pointer unchecked; the core establishes it only in net_rx_action(),
napi_threaded_poll_loop(), __napi_busy_loop(), busy_poll_stop(),
sch_handle_ingress/egress(), cpu_map_bpf_prog_run() and run_lwt_bpf().
An XDP hook driven from a bus callback rather than a NAPI poll gets
none of those, so any program calling bpf_redirect_map() -- including
libxdp's xsk_def_prog, which `xdp-loader load` installs by default --
oopsed on NULL+0x38 on the first datagram received:

  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at 0x38
  pc : xsk_map_redirect+0xc/0x90
  lr : bpf_prog_0718da224c8f0178_xsk_def_prog+0x5c/0x78
  Call trace:
    xsk_map_redirect / bpf_dispatcher_xdp_func
    mhi_process_data_event_ring [mhi] / mhi_ev_task [mhi]
    tasklet_action_common / handle_softirqs

Reflected XDP_TX frames get skb->protocol and the network header set
explicitly: they never traverse __netif_receive_skb_core(), which is
what normally does both, and without them cake_handle_diffserv() reads
protocol 0 and a bogus network offset — every reflection would land in
the besteffort tin with its DSCP ignored.

XDP_DROP is accounted to the core rx_dropped counter rather than
rx_errors: a policy drop is not a receive error, and conflating them
makes a healthily filtering link look faulty in `ip -s link`.
XDP_ABORTED and invalid verdicts still count as rx_errors.

Out-of-tree patch for the GL-X3000 lean build; applies after 991.

